      "content": "{\n  \"skill_name\": \"multi-agent-task-orchestrator\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"skills\": \"\\n## Skill: multi-agent-task-orchestrator\\n**Skill Path**: C:\\\\Users\\\\tostring\\\\.transmagent\\\\skills\\\\multi-agent-task-orchestrator\\n# Multi-Agent Task Orchestrator\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nA production-tested pattern for coordinating multiple AI agents through a single orchestrator. Instead of letting agents work independently (and conflict), one orchestrator decomposes tasks, routes them to specialists, prevents duplicate work, and verifies results before marking anything done. Battle-tested across 10,000+ tasks over 6 months.\\n\\n## Core Principles\\n\\n1. **Single Source of Truth**: One orchestrator holds the state; agents only execute specific subtasks.\\n2. **Anti-Duplication**: Before spawning any agent task, the orchestrator checks a central registry to ensure no identical task is already in-flight.\\n3. **Quality Gates**: Every agent output must pass a verification step (linting, schema validation, manual review flag) before being accepted.\\n4. **Heartbeat Monitoring**: If an agent doesn't report progress within 30 minutes, the orchestrator escalates or re-routes the task.\\n5. **Graceful Degradation**: If an agent fails, the orchestrator logs the failure, updates the task status, and optionally retries with a different agent.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n```mermaid\\ngraph TD\\n    Start((User Request)) --> O[Orchestrator]\\n    O --> D{Decompose Task}\\n    D -->|Subtask 1| Q1[Anti-Dup Check]\\n    D -->|Subtask 2| Q2[Anti-Dup Check]\\n    Q1 -->|No Duplicate| A1[Specialist Agent 1]\\n    Q2 -->|No Duplicate| A2[Specialist Agent 2]\\n    A1 --> V1{Quality Gate}\\n    A2 --> V2{Quality Gate}\\n    V1 -->|Pass| M[Merge Results]\\n    V1 -->|Fail| R1[Re-route / Retry]\\n    V2 -->|Pass| M\\n    V2 -->|Fail| R2[Re-route / Retry]\\n    M --> Final[Final Output]\\n```\\n\\n## Task Registration Format\\n\\nWhen registering a task with the orchestrator, use the following format:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"unique-task-id\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"analysis | generation | review | data-processing\\\",\\n  \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high | medium | low\\\",\\n  \\\"input\\\": \\\"description or reference\\\",\\n  \\\"required_agent\\\": \\\"agent-name or any\\\",\\n  \\\"quality_gate\\\": \\\"lint | schema | manual-review | none\\\",\\n  \\\"timeout_minutes\\\": 30\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Behavior Constraints\\n\\n- NEVER spawn two agents with identical task_id or task description.\\n- ALWAYS check the orchestrator's task registry before creating a new sub-agent.\\n- If a quality gate fails, update the task status to \\\"failed\\\" and log the reason.\\n- If an agent doesn't respond for >30 minutes, escalate the task to the orchestrator's pending queue.\\n- When merging results, prefer the output of higher-priority or more specialized agents.\\n\"\n}",
